On Jul 12, 3:33 pm, cdi <cdinchau...@hotmail.com> wrote:
> After reading both your 10-conduct YAAP and Rachel Dillon's 10-conduct
> YAAP, I'm forced to ask:  when doing a difficult conduct set, why
> monks?  The quest is horrible and even a non-conduct weaponless monk w/
> o drain life stands a decent chance of getting snuffed by Kaen.

If you try 10+ conducts, you can't do much of anything which is
usually done to prepare for the difficult tasks ahead.

I mean, lets look at intrinsics, maybe one of the major reasons to go
for monks. How can you get them? Eating, praying and crowning are most
likely forbidden by conducts. You can get some from eating of you are
vegan though. The monk just gets them all and that fairly reliable.
You start with a really nice set of them and get essentials like
poison resistance at lvl 3.

Lets look at killing things (if you are not even pacifist). Hitting
with a weapon is most likely out of the question, besides you can
neither pray or wish for a good one, nor enchant it properly (if
illiterate). Monks have no troubles with that either, just punch
everything down and your weapon gets better, with a bit of luck you
get gauntlets of power and you are fine. You could also kill by
casting spells but you have to change your strategy at turn count
20.000 then :D (again if illiterate).

Another point for "normal" characters is to acquire good body armor
quickly, but you can neither wish for dragon scale mails nor can you
produce one. As you also can't even enchant your armor very high you
will most likely end up with a crappy AC anyways. This doesn't
actually favor monks but makes one of their "weaknesses" void.

The quest artifact is pretty awesome, as it is a guaranteed source of
MR and the X-Ray vision helps in avoiding lots of troubles, especially
in the mazes. I don't know if this is extremely relevant at this point
in the game, but enlightenment will help you identify some of your
stuff.

Last but not least you start with a nice spell, which helps compensate
for loss of elbereth (when illiterate), etc.

Most things you would normally do with you char can't be done with 10+
conducts and monks simply either get the stuff for free or normally
don't use it anyways :D

